# GitHub Release Checklist — AU DIC v1.0.0

Use this checklist when publishing the official v1.0.0 release on GitHub.

---

## Pre-Release Verification

- [x] **Git Repository Clean**: No unstaged secrets or temporary runtime files.
- [x] **Benchmark Certification**: `benchmark_certificate.json` status is `PASS`.
- [x] **Manuscript Synchronization**: All numbers in `research_paper.md` match certified tables.
- [x] **Release Manifest**: `version1_release_manifest.md` generated and catalogued.
- [x] **Freeze Report**: `version1_freeze_report.md` signed off.

---

## Step-by-Step GitHub Publication Steps

### 1. Git Tag Creation
Execute in terminal at root directory:
```bash
git tag -a v1.0.0 -m "AU DIC Version 1.0.0 — Certified Workflow-Validation Release" 95dbb83
git push origin v1.0.0
```

### 2. GitHub Release UI Setup
1. Navigate to `https://github.com/aashishrajput9838/academicuniverse/releases/new`
2. Select tag: `v1.0.0`
3. Release Title: `Academic Universe Document Intelligence Core (AU DIC) v1.0.0`
4. Description: Copy content from `release_notes_v1.md`.

### 3. Attach Binary & Research Artifacts
Drag & drop the following zip package or files into the Release Assets section:
- [x] `research_paper.md`
- [x] `benchmark_certificate.json`
- [x] `experiment_VAL-20260729.json`
- [x] `version1_release_manifest.md`
- [x] `version1_freeze_report.md`

### 4. Metadata & Topics
Set repository topics:
`document-intelligence`, `multimodal-llm`, `gemini-api`, `human-in-the-loop`, `saas-architecture`, `benchmark-framework`, `reproducible-research`, `expressjs`, `nextjs`
